Lab 17: Satellite Content Synchronization and Promotion
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Configure and manage content synchronization across multiple Red Hat Satellite environments
Implement content promotion workflows between development, testing, and production lifecycle environments
Monitor and validate content promotion processes to ensure consistency and reliability
Troubleshoot common issues in content synchronization and promotion workflows
Understand best practices for managing content lifecycle in enterprise environments
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Red Hat Satellite Server architecture and concepts
Familiarity with Linux command line operations
Knowledge of package management concepts (RPM, repositories)
Understanding of software development lifecycle environments (dev, test, prod)
Basic networking concepts and SSH connectivity
Previous experience with Red Hat Satellite content management (recommended)
