Task 1: Configure Content Synchronization Across Environments
Subtask 1.1: Verify Satellite Server Configuration
First, let's verify that our Satellite server is properly configured and running.

Connect to the Satellite server:
ssh root@satellite-server
Check Satellite services status:
satellite-maintain service status
Verify Satellite version and health:
satellite-maintain health check
List existing organizations and locations:
hammer organization list
hammer location list
Subtask 1.2: Create Lifecycle Environments
Now we'll create the three lifecycle environments: Development, Testing, and Production.

Create Development lifecycle environment:
hammer lifecycle-environment create \
  --name "Development" \
  --description "Development Environment" \
  --prior "Library" \
  --organization "Default Organization"
Create Testing lifecycle environment:
hammer lifecycle-environment create \
  --name "Testing" \
  --description "Testing Environment" \
  --prior "Development" \
  --organization "Default Organization"
Create Production lifecycle environment:
hammer lifecycle-environment create \
  --name "Production" \
  --description "Production Environment" \
  --prior "Testing" \
  --organization "Default Organization"
Verify lifecycle environments:
hammer lifecycle-environment list --organization "Default Organization"
Subtask 1.3: Configure Content Repositories
Set up repositories that will be synchronized across environments.

Create a product for RHEL content:
hammer product create \
  --name "RHEL8-Content" \
  --description "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8 Content" \
  --organization "Default Organization"
Add RHEL 8 BaseOS repository:
hammer repository create \
  --name "RHEL8-BaseOS" \
  --product "RHEL8-Content" \
  --content-type "yum" \
  --url "https://cdn.redhat.com/content/dist/rhel8/8/x86_64/baseos/os" \
  --organization "Default Organization"
Add RHEL 8 AppStream repository:
hammer repository create \
  --name "RHEL8-AppStream" \
  --product "RHEL8-Content" \
  --content-type "yum" \
